findings.scenario:
On edge-bff (the beta), three keys are references to other services:
- TERMINAL_PROXY_KEY = ${{terminal-api.TERMINAL_PROXY_KEY}}
- BACKTEST_WORKER_KEY = ${{backtest-worker.BACKTEST_WORKER_KEY}}
- SCREENER_WORKER_KEY = ${{screener-worker.SCREENER_WORKER_KEY}}

edge-bff-live holds ${{edge-bff.<same name>}} for each, so each is a chain of two references.

Take a rotation of the gateway key at terminal-api, done as M308 says (BACKTEST_WORKER_KEY was rotated this way on 2026-11-16). `railway_reference_consumers.py terminal-api.TERMINAL_PROXY_KEY --redeploy` lists and redeploys only edge-bff. edge-bff-live keeps the value resolved at its last deploy (M308: a consumer left undeployed keeps the old value).
- terminal-api then refuses it with 401 proxy_key_rejected, so every visitor's Terminal fails. In pre-launch that is the only thing the site offers.
- After a worker-key rotation, the live Backtest or Screener fail the same way.
- /ready stays 200 because it reads only the database, so nothing flags the fault.

